      "title": "RosterConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SetupConfig": {
      "description": "Which rows of the «Einrichtung» card this station ticked off by hand.\n\nThe card derives every row from the document itself, but some rows can never become true\nthat way — a station happy with the built-in vehicles never writes ``fleet.vehicles``, so\nthat row would nag forever. A hand tick is the escape hatch, and it belongs in the document\nrather than on the device: «erledigt» is a statement about the Wehr, and the next admin on\nthe next tablet has to see it.",
      "properties": {
        "acknowledged": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Acknowledged",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "title": "SetupConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SharePointConfig": {
      "description": "Where this deployment pulls station data from, and how often. Read-only, pull-only.\n\n⚠️ NO CREDENTIAL LIVES HERE. ``GET /api/config`` is public and the Sicherung round-trip\nreplaces this document wholesale; the tenant/client id and the client secret are in the\nencrypted credential store (app/credentials · the ``sharepoint`` group). What stays in the\ndocument is the part an operator wants to read back, diff and version: which folders.",
      "properties": {
        "intervalMinutes": {
          "default": 60,
          "maximum": 10080,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Intervalminutes",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "sources": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SharePointSource"
          },
          "title": "Sources",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "title": "SharePointConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SharePointSource": {
      "description": "One area's folder in SharePoint — where to look, for what kind of data.\n\nEvery field but ``area`` is about ADDRESSING, and the addressing is per source on purpose:\na station that keeps its Objektpläne on the Kommando site and its Geodaten in a different\nlibrary configures two entries with two ``siteUrl``s. Nothing here requires a common root,\nand an area a station does not have is simply not listed.\n\nPoint at the site with ``siteUrl`` (the address out of a browser's URL bar,\n``https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/feuerwehr``) and this deployment resolves it to the\ndocument library itself; give ``driveId`` instead when a tenant admin has handed over the\nlibrary id directly. ``library`` picks a non-default document library by its display name.\n``path`` is the folder INSIDE that library — the per-area naming convention from\ndocs/sharepoint-connector.md applies below it, never above it.\n\n``ignore`` names the sub-folders the pull walks past — the category folders every grown\ndocument library has («Grosspläne», «Archiv»), which are not Einsatzobjekte and must never\nbecome one.",
      "properties": {
        "area": {
          "enum": [
            "plans",
            "geodata",
            "checklists",
            "workbook"
          ],
          "title": "Area",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "siteUrl": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Siteurl"
        },
        "driveId": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Driveid"
        },
        "library": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Library"
        },
        "path": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Path",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "ignore": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Ignore",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "area"
      ],
      "title": "SharePointSource",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
